Lum: one 38 px bar instead of Chromium's tab strip + toolbar (docs/lum-ui-spec.md, "Bar").

- No horizontal tab strip in normal windows: the toolbar moves up next to the window
  buttons (Chromium's own no-tab-strip layout). Tabs: Ctrl+T / Ctrl+W / Ctrl+Tab for now,
  Lum's tabs in the bar come in a later patch.
- The bar shows only back, forward, reload and the address. Chromium's other toolbar
  controls stay alive (so features anchored to them keep working) but take no space and
  are fully transparent. No overflow menu.
- The address is plain centered text (host bright, the rest dimmed), no icons around it,
  no placeholder.
- 38 x 38 buttons touching each other, no side padding.
- Window buttons in Lum's "Round" style: arc down (green), arc up (yellow), circle (red),
  no hover background.
- Colors of the default "Black" theme: black bar, light icons and text, no hover fills.

